%U A397965 1314506572993696005373455864,69817563779396112668041084455747,8033200660573962192553336867393959344,1990641368107873255528259447300281539482701
%N A397965 Number of pairs (D, h) where D is a digraph on n labeled nodes and h elects one node in each source SCC of D (an SCC receiving no external edge) such that attaching a virtual root joined to the elected nodes yields a reducible flow graph.
%C A397965 Reducibility of a digraph is not root-free: a strongly connected digraph can be reducible from one choice of entry and irreducible from another (smallest example on 3 nodes: edges 12, 13, 23, 32, 21 -- reducible rooted at node 2 or 3, irreducible at node 1), so general digraphs are classified by ELECTIONS of source-SCC headers.
%C A397965 Equivalently: every non-source SCC of D has a unique entry node and is reducible from it, and every source SCC is reducible from its elected node; elections of distinct source SCCs are independent.
%C A397965 Exact recurrence: the (digraph, election) pairs are the acyclic header-entering assemblies of pointed reducible regions without the root-reachability requirement; i.e., Sum_k D(n,k) over the assembly table of the reducible flow graph recurrence.
%C A397965 Digraphs reducible for SOME election number 1, 4, 60, 3008, 449440; for EVERY election 1, 4, 54, 1916, 155840 (n <= 5).  Those graph counts reduce exactly to the number of strong digraphs with at least one / with all valid headers; both kernels and the pair count are finite closed computations.
%H A397965 Matthew S. Hecht and Jeffrey D. Ullman, <a href="https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/800152.804919">Flow graph reducibility</a>, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202. Proc. 4th Ann. ACM Symp. Theory of Comput. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1145/800152.804919">(STOC '72)</a>, 238-250.
%H A397965 Matthew S. Hecht and Jeffrey D. Ullman, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1145/321832.32183">Characterizations of reducible flow graphs</a>, J. ACM 21(3) (1974), 367-375.
%H A397965 R. W. Robinson, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1142/2822">Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components</a>, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%H A397965 Robert E. Tarjan, <a href="https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/800125.804040">Testing flow graph reducibility</a>, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365. Proc. 5th Ann. ACM Symp. Theory of Comput. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1145/800125.804040">(STOC '73)</a>, 96-107.
%F A397965 a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n} D(n,k), where D(n,k) counts acyclic assemblies of k pointed reducible SCC regions on n labeled vertices, with every cross-region edge entering the header of its target region.
%o A397965 (Python) reducible_labeled_system(14)[3] # See Python link in A398465 for program code.
